From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH kbase-common 014] panvk: query fd properties without GPU import

Purpose: panvk_GetMemoryFdPropertiesKHR() performs a full transient GPU
 import (kbase mappings + mmaps) per query just to derive memory type
 bits, then frees it. On this DDK, repeated import/free cycles of the
 same dma-buf alias to one GPU VA, and the frees (EINVAL) tear down GPU
 PTEs that re-import does not restore: the subsequent REAL import hits
 a dead VA and the GPU faults (TRANSLATION_FAULT) on first access.
 Compute (no queries) and vendor (single import, no query churn) work;
 every failing flow (AHB, fd-import) queries first.
 For kbase devices, answer from the same flag assumptions the import
 path uses (kmod_flags=0 + IMPORTED: visible + coherent, not cached)
 without creating any GPU mapping. Behavior-preserving for the reported
 bits; eliminates the churn entirely. Also validate that fd is non-negative
 and seekable before reporting success.
Source/Reference: G615 bring-up forensics (ioctl trace: 3x aliased
 IMPORT 0x41000 + EINVAL FREEs + TRANSLATION_FAULT; vendor: 1x IMPORT,
 no fault).
Tested GPU: Poco X6 Pro / G615 (Gate G).
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.21.
Mesa base range: 26.3.0-devel (pinned 5a07217f).
Dependencies: 004 (kbase_node_path).
Validation test: Gate G (single IMPORT per AHB, GPU clear lands).

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_device_memory.c
@@ -479,5 +479,37 @@
    assert(handleType == VK_EXTERNAL_MEMORY_HANDLE_TYPE_DMA_BUF_BIT_EXT);
 
+#if defined(HAVE_PAN_KMOD_KBASE)
+   /* On kbase, a full transient import per query is not free: repeated
+    * import/free cycles of one dma-buf alias to a single GPU VA, and the
+    * frees can tear down GPU PTEs that re-import does not restore,
+    * breaking the later real import (GPU TRANSLATION_FAULT). Answer from
+    * the same assumptions the fd-import path uses instead.
+    */
+   if (phys_dev->kbase_node_path[0]) {
+      if (fd < 0 || lseek(fd, 0, SEEK_END) < 0)
+         return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
+
+      /* Matches kbase_kmod_bo_import_fd(..., kmod_flags=0, external): */
+      const bool can_do_host_visible = true;
+      const bool can_do_host_coherent = true;
+      const bool can_do_host_cached = false;
+      pMemoryFdProperties->memoryTypeBits = 0;
+      for (uint32_t i = 0; i < phys_dev->memory.type_count; i++) {
+         if (!can_do_host_visible && (phys_dev->memory.types[i].propertyFlags &
+                                      VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_VISIBLE_BIT))
+            continue;
+         if (!can_do_host_coherent && (phys_dev->memory.types[i].propertyFlags &
+                                       VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_COHERENT_BIT))
+            continue;
+         if (!can_do_host_cached && (phys_dev->memory.types[i].propertyFlags &
+                                     VK_MEMORY_PROPERTY_HOST_CACHED_BIT))
+            continue;
+         pMemoryFdProperties->memoryTypeBits |= BITFIELD_BIT(i);
+      }
+      return VK_SUCCESS;
+   }
+#endif
+
    struct pan_kmod_bo *bo = pan_kmod_bo_import(device->kmod.dev, fd);
    if (!bo)
       return VK_ERROR_INVALID_EXTERNAL_HANDLE;
